[36m(TaskRunner pid=1546835)[0m     "snippet": "---\ntitle: 14 Pairs of Actors Who Were Born to Appear Together in the Same Movies\nauthor: This Is A Placeholder\ndate: 2014-01-01\n---\nKeanu Reeves and Charlize Theron!\n\n14 Pairs of Actors Who Were Born to Appear Together in the Same Movies\n\nCharlie Chaplin and Edna Purviance starred in more than 30 movies together. Some actors have such great chemistry that directors want to see them together more than once. And we totally agree with them, because some duos are just meant to be together, even if only in a fictional reality.\n\nHere at Bright Side, we love movies. This time, we want to highlight the best movie duos who stole our hearts more than once.\n\n1. Emma Stone and Ryan Gosling\n\nEmma Stone and Ryan Gosling first appeared together in 2011 in Crazy, Stupid, Love and totally won our hearts from the very beginning. Fortunately, they paired perfectly: Emma said that she loved working with Ryan so much that she wanted to make as many movies with him as she could.\n\nIt seems like her wish was granted. After that, they played a couple 2 more times: in 2013 in Gangster Squad and again in 2016 in La La Land.\n\n2. Kate Winslet and Leonardo DiCaprio\n\nKate Winslet and Leonardo DiCaprio first met on the set of Titanic in 1997. They developed a very strong friendship and have been ever-present in each other's lives since then. Leonardo even walked Kate down the aisle on her wedding day. 11 years after the release of Titanic, they played a married couple in the movie Revolutionary Road.\n\n3. Angelina Jolie and Brad Pitt\n\nThis unforgettable duo first appeared together in 2005 in Mr. & Mrs. Smith. These actors fell in love with each other on set and now they are parents to 6 children: both biological and adopted. 10 years later, they appeared together again in the movie By the Sea, written and directed by Angelina Jolie herself.\n\n4. Saoirse Ronan and Timoth\u00e9e Chalamet\n\nAnother favorite duo was born in 2017 with the movie Lady Bird. Timoth\u00e9e and Saoirse are close friends in real life and a great match on set. Timoth\u00e9e said that with Saoirse, he sometimes doesn't even feel like he's"
